Run instructions
Save each script separately in your Debian VM:
nano kernel_hardening.sh


Paste Script 1, save, then:
sudo bash kernel_hardening.sh


Repeat for:
nano firewall_ufw.sh
sudo bash firewall_ufw.sh


And:
nano sshd_hardening.sh
sudo bash sshd_hardening.sh


Final verification
After all three:
sysctl kernel.randomize_va_space
sudo ufw status verbose
sudo sshd -t
sudo sshd -T | grep -E 'permitrootlogin|passwordauthentication|usepam'
systemctl is-enabled ssh
systemctl is-active ssh


My recommended order: kernel → SSH → firewall. Run them from the VM's local console, keep your existing administrator session open, and check the CyberPatriot scoring report afterward.

The kernel script is supplemental hardening, not a guaranteed scoring item from your README. The SSH and UFW scripts directly address explicit README requirements.
